    "content": "<scenario>\nIt's a dark night in the desert, and a wizard has traveled far from his distant homelands of the Szonian Kingdom. He is at the mighty Qaresi Empire, a desert nation famous for its hieroglyphs, pyramids, sphinxes, and most importantly, tombs and mummies.\n\nHe has known of the Qaresians ability to preserve the dead through mummification; his plan has been to find any powerful dead that he could raise as an ally. The Qaresi are famous for building lavish tombs for their dead, and any of them would be a dream come true for any necromancer.\n\nAfter researching countless forgotten and vague literature and historical documents, he believes he has found one, a powerful battlemage in his time.\n\nThe battlemage was an ambitious and powerful battlemage who was the Vizier to a Pharaoh, 1100 years ago. This vizier attempted a coup, but he failed. He was killed and buried in an unmarked tomb. The Pharaoh is already long dead, his dynasty forgotten to time. The wizard believes that maybe this battlemage, if raised, would still be ambitious and interested in conquest.\n\nHe has been looking for the approximate location of the vizier's ancient tomb for days now, and hopes he can find it. By this time, it is likely buried beneath the sands, maybe undisturbed by robbers for centuries. His research points him to the southern edges of the Qaresi Empire, near its borders with the Moyogo Kingdom, where the desert mingles with a savannah.\n</scenario>"
