    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "“**GYAAAAAAGH!**”\n\nThe magister's muscles spasmed, then locked. His hands clenched and his legs seized as the nyw's electrical discharge tore through him. Bolts overwhelmed the wizard and dominated the entire chamber in a flash, as if the end of the world was brought upon them.\n\nAnd with the end of the world, the magister was thrown twenty feet backward, crashing through a pillar and landing on a pile of rubble. Through the darkness, his hands blindly sought his belt, finding only empty loops of leather where his pouches had been.\n\nStill mildly shocked by this creature's capabilities, he squinted his eyes as his vision slowly cleared. His bag had been flung several feet away—his research, summoning scrolls, phylacteries, *everything*. Beside it, the gold-etched rings that were on his fingers had scattered across the stone floor like fallen stars.\n\nThe ostrich rushed forward, its eyes fixed on the glittering prizes.\n\n“No!” The magister scrambled up; he had to stop this thief. “**Glacial Shard-Burst!**”\n\nWith a desperate incantation, he channeled his *palla*. A ball of spiked ice erupted from his palms and shrieked through the air toward the satchel. He expected the bird to be impaled dead on, its stupid little life extinguished.\n\nThe ice sphere surged through the air, but missed its mark. It grazed the nyw’s side, the spikes tearing through its feathers and drawing streaks of red. Instead of charging the pouch, the bird had veered toward the scattered rings. Had it not, it would have certainly been served frozen.\n\nAmidst chirps of pain, the nyw leaned down. Its beak snapped twice—*click-click*—and snatched both rings clean off the ground and turned on its heel. It scrambled back toward the chambers leading to the collapsed ceiling.\n\n“Curse you! Curse this wretched land and its ridiculous beasts!” Heavy jumps echoed through the tunnel, the sounds growing fainter as the creature leapt and fled toward the desert. *Fine. Then have them, you fowl creature. Gold is plentiful; knowledge is not.*\n\nHe took a moment to compose himself, smoothing his dusted cloak and regaining his dignity. Soon after, he cast the light spell again and the glow once again brought life to the decrepit chambers. His fingers closed around the leather strap of his knapsack. All remained intact—notes, scrolls, valuables.\n\nStepping forward, he moved deeper into the heart of the tomb, leaving the destruction behind. The murals continued, much like before. The scenes of conquest and statecraft were precisely what his research had promised—a testament to a man who understood the mechanics of power. His sources spoke of Sutentet the Vizier, the Battlemage, the Traitor, but they had been conspicuously silent on Sutentet the man.\n\nThe elf's interest, however, was piqued by the unfamiliar. A mural at the far end of the hall depicted another figure.\n\nWho this one was, was clear. Not a god, but perhaps the closest one can be to such a thing in this land."
