    "content": "*Pharaoh Zarantep V.*\n\nThe leader of that ancient era, depicted at the height of his power. \"So this is the man Sutentet once served,\" the elf muttered as he examined the ruler's painted face. \"A man who clearly enjoyed his own reflection, and the man who was his executioner.\"\n\nBut it was the five forms near the royal that drew his keen interest. They were smaller than the Pharaoh but stood in precise ranks, and they were not simple courtiers. He knew, from his research, who they really were.\n\n*The Royal Medjay.* The Pharaoh's four elite bodyguards of that time, a retinue that still exists in the present.\n\nThe elf studied each one, and even he could admit they were formidable.\n\nFirst, a mountain of muscle. An orc with long, flowing hair and a massive battleaxe rested on one shoulder. _Brute. A gladiator made nobleman, surely._ Next to him stood another that drew his eye. A dark elf with skin the color of a deep twilight sky. He wore a sleek black robe trimmed in delicate gold, and in his hand, he gripped an enchanted khopesh. _An assassin. He hadsthe look of someone who enjoys the kill more than the victory. I can respect that._\n\nThen came an older man with black turban and robes, his face etched with lines that suggested wisdom and years of conflict. Two daggers hung at his waist, and wisps of magical energy were swirled around him. _Looks like a battlemage of some repute. Seems even back then the Qaresi seemed to know a little bit of magical qi._\n\nFinally, there were two figures at the end of the line, holding hands. Both clad in white silk robes and each held a staff. The qi aura enveloping them felt vivid enough that the magister could feel its power through the painting. _And two wizards to round it out. A matching set of arcane practitioners._\n\nThe magister stepped back, counting them once more. \"One orc, one dark elf, one elder, and two wizards… that makes five.\" The eyes of the dark elf seemed to challenge his skepticism. The elf traced the lines of the the finer hieroglyphs, translating aloud. “His Majesty and his four esteemed Medjay…”\n\n“So, the Qaresi can build pyramids that challenge the skies, but they cannot master simple arithmetic?” He shook his head and chuckled at the perceived stupidity of the ancient civilization. “Did they count their guards twice or simply forget what a number was once the desert sun got too hot?”\n\n At the other end of the wall, two other murals told the rest of the story."
